New prerequisite evidence:
The embedded configuration was extracted from the exact reused kernel payload using scripts/extract-ikconfig; saved as snapshot26-kernel.config:
  CONFIG_TMPFS=y
  # CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR is not set
  CONFIG_EXT4_FS_SECURITY=y
  CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
The debug policy declares (fsuse trans tmpfs ...), line 72.
Local security/selinux/hooks.c is byte-identical to Android common android16-6.12 commit 3a7d1771d4925a56f7eeb8a5ba1faff0c544a9ef (verified against decoded online source).
- selinux_inode_setsecurity(), lines 3493-3506, rejects filesystems not yet marked SBLABEL_MNT with EOPNOTSUPP.
- inode_doinit_with_dentry(), lines 1514-1523, initializes SECURITY_FS_USE_TRANS labels through a transition, not by reading stored xattrs.
- mm/shmem.c lines 4813-4815 only install shmem xattr handlers with CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR.
The capture reports errno95 at the enclosing guard step, not the exact syscall. Unsupported pre-policy tmpfs labeling is source-supported; do not claim the log individually identifies fsetxattr versus another xattr operation.
Simply enabling TMPFS_XATTR would not by itself establish label preservation under fsuse trans.
Source: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/3a7d1771d4925a56f7eeb8a5ba1faff0c544a9ef/security/selinux/hooks.c

Next bounded candidate, NOT applied or verified:
Use Android init's existing post-policy /dev restorecon rather than pre-policy tmpfs xattrs. Retain staging paths and grant init relabelfrom on tmpfs regular files, and relabelto on the two required target types. Label staged vendor contexts as file_contexts_file and staged fstab as vendor_configs_file. Existing policy already associates file_type with tmpfs. This needs explicit approval, policy validation, and a new temporary boot; it must not be described as a proven fix.

Earlier evidence correction:
ack-screen-logdump-20261007.bin matches its 48484-byte .log prefix exactly. At that boundary, a partial old record and sequence602 at an older timestamp resume. The previously generated ack-ssd-context-logdump-20261007-full.log contains stale tail data and must not be treated as one current boot. The permissive=1 AVC alone does not prove which logger syscall failed.
